  "title": "Erdős Problem #644",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $f(k,r)$ be minimal such that if $A_1,A_2,\\ldots$ is a family of sets, all of size $k$, such that for every collection of $r$ of the $A_is$ there is some pair $\\{x,y\\}$ which intersects all of the $A_j$, then there is some set of size $f(k,r)$ which intersects all of the sets $A_i$. Is it true that $ f(k,7)=(1+o(1))\\frac{3}{4}k? $ Is it true that for any $r\\geq 3$ there exists some constant $c_r$ such that $ f(k,r)=(1+o(1))c_rk? $ ",
